 "summary": {
  "version": 1,
  "basis": "em",
  "attribution": "Written by a model from the explanatory memorandum; not the record",
  "describes_version": "original",
  "as_of": "2013-11-13",
  "sentences": [
   "Part of a 13-bill package, this bill would ban price exploitation and misleading claims about prices after the carbon tax is repealed.",
   "The bill would create a new offence with fines of up to 6,471 penalty units for companies and 1,295 for individuals, and give the ACCC powers to monitor prices during the transition.",
   "The ACCC would check whether savings from the repeal are passed on to consumers, especially in markets where competition is limited."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Introduce a new prohibition on price exploitation related to the carbon tax repeal for key goods like electricity and gas.",
   "Give the ACCC monitoring powers to assess the effect of the repeal on prices.",
   "Ban false or misleading representations about how the carbon tax repeal affects prices."
  ],
  "affected": "Businesses supplying key goods such as electricity and gas, and their customers.",
